hon Developer Salary in India for Freshers<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The salary of fresher Python developers in India is \u20b93 Lakh Per Annum (LPA). It can vary on the basis of the company, location of the job, and level of candidate skills.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It is safe to say that a Python developer&#8217;s salary structure and career advancement go hand-in-hand.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Python Developer Salary For 2-3 Years of Experience<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The salary of experienced developers increases as they upgrade their skills and gain exposure.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>According to <a href=\"https:\/\/www.ambitionbox.com\/profile\/python-developer-salary\">AmbitionBox<\/a>, the average salary of a Python developer having 2 to 3 years of experience is \u20b94.1 Lakh Per Annum (LPA).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Python Developer Salary After 5 Years<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The salary of Python developers having experience of 4 to 9 years of experience is \u20b98.2 Lakh Per Annum (LPA).&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Python Developer Salary in India in Different Companies in 2026<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>A Python developer can earn a good salary in India. But the salary depends on several factors, including years of experience, location, and specific company.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Here is a breakdown of average salaries by companies hiring Python developers in India.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table is-style-regular\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Name of Company<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Average Salary Paid<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Infosys<\/td><td>\u20b94.8 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Google&nbsp;<\/td><td>\u20b938 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Zoho<\/td><td>\u20b95.6 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TCS<\/td><td>\u20b94.9 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>HCL<\/td><td>\u20b95.9 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Tech Mahindra<\/td><td>\u20b95.3 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Cognizant<\/td><td>\u20b95.9 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>IBM<\/td><td>\u20b95.4 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Wipro<\/td><td>\u20b95.1 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Capgemini<\/td><td>\u20b96.4 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Accenture<\/td><td>\u20b95.7 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Deloitte<\/td><td>\u20b99.5 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>JP Morgan Chase<\/td><td>\u20b99.8 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>E&amp;Y<\/td><td>\u20b98.2 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Amazon<\/td><td>\u20b920 LPA<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Python Developer Salary in India in Different Locations or Cities<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The salary a full-stack Python developer receive varies based on the city. Factors such as the cost of livelihood, relocation costs, and rampant competition among candidates influence the variation in the salary structure in India.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Here\u2019s a table depicting the Python developer\u2019s highest salaries in different cities in India.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>City Name<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Average Salary Paid<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Bangalore<\/td><td>\u20b96.6 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Chennai<\/td><td>\u20b95.4 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Mumbai<\/td><td>\u20b95.7 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Pune&nbsp;<\/td><td>\u20b95.4 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Hyderabad<\/td><td>\u20b94.7 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>New Delhi<\/td><td>\u20b96.0 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Noida<\/td><td>\u20b94.8 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Gurgaon<\/td><td>\u20b97.0 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Kolkatta<\/td><td>\u20b97.0 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Ahmedabad&nbsp;<\/td><td>\u20b96.8 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Jaipur<\/td><td>\u20b96.1 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Indore<\/td><td>\u20b93.5 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Chandigarh<\/td><td>\u20b97.0 LPA<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Lucknow<\/td><td>\u20b93.8 LPA<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also read: <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/full-stack-developer-salary-in-india\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Full Stack Developer Salary in India: Monthly &amp; Annual<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highest Paying Cities for Python Developers<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Here is a list of some of the cities that are known to offer some of the highest Python developer salaries, along with an explanation of why they are considered hotspots for Python development and high salaries:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Bengaluru (Bangalore)<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Salaries<\/strong>: Bengaluru consistently ranks as one of the highest paying cities for Python developers in India. Salaries for Python developers in Bengaluru can be significantly higher than the national average.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Tech Hub<\/strong>: Bengaluru is often referred to as the &#8220;Silicon Valley of India&#8221; due to its thriving tech ecosystem. It hosts numerous IT companies, startups, and multinational corporations, creating a high demand for Python developers.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Hyderabad<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Salaries<\/strong>: Hyderabad offers competitive salaries for Python developers, making it an attractive destination. Salaries in the city are often on par with or slightly below Bengaluru.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Emerging IT Hub<\/strong>: Hyderabad has emerged as a major IT hub in India, with a growing number of tech companies establishing a presence there. The availability of office space and a skilled workforce has contributed to this growth.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Quality of Life<\/strong>: The city&#8217;s relatively lower cost of living compared to some other major cities makes it an appealing choice for Python developers seeking a balance between salary and expenses.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Pune<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Salaries<\/strong>: Pune offers competitive salaries for Python developers, and the cost of living is relatively lower than in cities like Bengaluru and Mumbai.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>IT and Education<\/strong>: Pune has a strong IT sector, with a significant number of IT parks and software companies. Additionally, it&#8217;s known for its educational institutions, producing a steady supply of tech talent.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Mumbai<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Salaries<\/strong>: Mumbai, as India&#8217;s financial capital, offers attractive Python developer salaries. While the cost of living is high, the compensation often aligns with the city&#8217;s living standards.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Diverse Industries<\/strong>: Mumbai&#8217;s diverse economy includes finance, entertainment, and tech. Python developers in Mumbai often work in finance-related technology roles, where expertise in Python is highly valued.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Gurgaon and Noida (Delhi NCR)<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Salaries<\/strong>: The Delhi National Capital Region (NCR), including Gurgaon and Noida, offers competitive salaries for Python developers, with many tech companies and startups operating in this region.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Tech Corridor<\/strong>: The NCR region is home to a thriving tech corridor with numerous IT parks and multinational companies. It has witnessed rapid growth in the IT and software development sectors.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">6. Chennai<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Salaries<\/strong>: Chennai offers competitive salaries for Python developers, and the city has a lower cost of living compared to some other major cities.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>IT and Automotive<\/strong>: Chennai has a strong presence in the IT sector,